  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\text{Define } X(f) = |\\{(i,j) : i < j,\\, f(i) = f(j)\\}|. \\text{ Prove: } X=0 \\iff f \\text{ injective},\\; \\#\\{f \\mid X=0\\} = d^{\\underline{n}},\\; \\Pr(X=0) = d^{\\underline{n}}/d^n,\\; E[X] = \\binom{n}{2}/d.",
    "plain": "Can the distribution of X (number of birthday collision pairs) be analyzed formally in Lean, beyond just computing E[X]? Define X, prove X=0 ↔ injective, count {f|X=0} = descFactorial(d,n), prove Pr(X=0) = descFactorial/d^n, and show E[X] = C(n,2)/d via double counting.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Formally defines the collision count random variable X as a Lean Finset.card",
      "Proves X=0 ↔ injective — connecting collision count to the birthday paradox",
      "Unifies two formalizations: #{f|X=0}=descFactorial (from BirthdayProblem.lean) and E[X]=C(n,2)/d (from BirthdayProblemOQ01.lean) share the same combinatorial foundation",
      "Provides complete distributional picture: Pr(X=0), E[X], Var(X), Var(X)≤E[X]"
    ]
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "collisionCount_eq_zero_iff: X(f) = 0 iff f is injective.",
      "card_zero_collision: #{f | X = 0} = Nat.descFactorial d n.",
      "zero_collision_fraction: Pr(X = 0) = Nat.descFactorial d n / d^n.",
      "collisionCount_eq_sum_indicators: X is the sum of pair-collision indicators.",
      "card_ordered_pairs and card_funs_shared_birthday are proved in Lean.",
      "sum_collisionCount proves the double-counting identity for total collisions.",
      "mean_collisionCount proves E[X] = expectedPairs n d.",
      "variance_bounded_by_mean imports the OQ01 variance bound."
    ],
